From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:14:34 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] engine: office command-hook seam on Session::execute

office_hook.rs adds a process-wide CommandHook (before: a reason to refuse a command; after: the
outcome of one that ran). Session::execute asks it for the outermost command of an action only, and
the UI greys a control out through ribbon::enabled and refuses the three paths that bypass the
dispatcher on the web (export, print, save as). With no hook attached nothing changes: tests assert
that a command's result is byte-identical.
